  "worked_solution": "Let's examine our statement:\n\n- The word \"every\" indicates we should use a universal quantifier, $\u2200.$\n\n- The sentence refers to integers. So, by denoting an integer number as $x,$ we have that \n\n$$\n\u2200\\,x\\in Z.\n$$\n\n- Finally, the condition in the statement can be written as \n\n$$\nx\\text{\u00a0is even or\u00a0}x\\text{\u00a0is odd}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we write the statement as follows: \n\n$\u2200\\,x\\in Z,\\,x$ is even or $x$ is odd.",
